<title>JAPAN: Amsc to market Motorola's contactless chip cards.</title>
<headline>Amsc to market Motorola's contactless chip cards.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amsc Co Ltd, a Japanese trading firm of semiconductors, said on Thursday that it has signed an agreement with Motorola Inc's Japanese unit to market Motorola's contactless chip card systems which can be used in distribution systems.</p>
<p>In the system, the data stored in the cards, which incorporate integrated circuit chips, can be read without inserting the card into a machine.</p>
<p>The system was developed by another Motorola affiliate, Motorola Indala Corp.</p>
